{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T17:21:33.908Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. All seven `tests/report-index.test.ts` tests pass, and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, UI build, full test suite, lint) passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the read-index connection on top of task 1's `stream-index.ts`:\n\n- **`src/core/report/stream-reads.ts`**: `withStreamReads(work, index?)` carries an optional `StreamIndex` in the scope. `readEventStream` stats a covered path, returns re-frozen indexed events on a size/mtime hit, and on a miss reads/parses/stores. Non-covered paths and `readParsedFile` are unchanged; events stay frozen and log-free in both cases.\n- **`src/core/report/report.ts`**: new `MetricsReportOptions` (extends `InboxWaitOptions` with `index?: boolean`, default false). `getMetricsReport` with `index: true` opens the index for the change tree's archive folder before the scope and closes it in a `finally`, falling back to files if the index can't open.\n- **`src/cli/report.ts`**: `reportCommand` now passes `index: true`.\n- **`decisions/008-sqlite-read-index.md`** + README index line.\n- **`tests/report-index.test.ts`**: cold/warm deep equality, warm run reading no archived event stream, plus deleted/corrupt/locked/appended-line/removed-archive scenarios.\n\nOne note recorded in the result: the warm-read assertion counts archived *event streams* (`.run/events/*.jsonl`), since `plan.jsonl` is deliberately not indexed per the proposal."}}
